-- ============================================================================
-- EC3 PROFESSIONAL DEEP SEED: Probabilistic Economics, intermediate tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json rather than hand typed.
--
-- What this tier owns: PERCENTILES DONE PROPERLY, on the Probabilistic
-- Breakeven Analyzer. Three stated percentiles fitted to a triangular whose
-- CDF passes through all three; sampling by the inverse CDF through a seeded
-- generator, three draws in a fixed order; the breakeven price by bisection
-- on a monotone NPV with a kink wherever a year's tax switches on; reading
-- the sample as percentiles of a price; and a tornado with both sides.
--
-- THE TRAP THE TIER IS BUILT ON. Stated 10th, 50th and 90th percentiles are
-- NOT a minimum, mode and maximum. Feeding them in as endpoints deletes the
-- outer twenty percent of the distribution and understates every downside,
-- and the fitted triangle is always wider than the belief it honours.
--
-- THE ENGINE FACTS THIS TIER OWNS. Some beliefs no triangular can honour:
-- the shape ratio (50th minus 10th over 90th minus 10th) must sit strictly
-- inside the band a triangle can reach, and outside it the fit clamps and
-- says so. A breakeven price is a quantity where more is worse, so it is
-- described by percentiles and never by P-labels. Efficiency runs backwards:
-- its higher percentile gives the lower breakeven.
--
-- The only numbers that travel from this tier to the next are the fitted
-- distributions and the percentile summary of the breakeven price.
-- ============================================================================

